X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Californiabluegrass": "https://californiabluegrass.org/event/thomas-cassell-and-nick-at-out-west-garage/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:californiabluegrass
X-SOURCE:California Bluegrass Association
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T220000
DTSTAMP:20260906T024704Z
CREATED:20260906T023456Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260906T024704Z
UID:348674-1789239600-1789250400@californiabluegrass.org
SUMMARY:Thomas Cassell and Nick Fallon at Out West Garage
DESCRIPTION:Originally from the sacred bluegrass mountains of southwestern Virginia\, Thomas Cassell stands among the top tier of modern bluegrass musicians. A member of the Wood Box Heroes\, he’s made numerous Grand Ole Opry appearances\, in addition to building an accomplished history as a sideman with artists such as Trey Hensley\, Nefesh Mountain\, Billy Strings\, Bryan Sutton\, and more. \nCassell’s most recent album release\, Guitar Collection (2026)\, highlights an impressive roster of collaborators with each of its tracks featuring a different guest artist\, including Tim Stafford\, Trey Hensley\, Nick Fallon\, and more. \nNick Fallon is a progressive bluegrass guitarist\, singer\, and songwriter from Floyd\, Virginia\, now making his mark in Nashville’s vibrant acoustic scene\, having toured extensively across the U.S. and internationally as a member of the acclaimed Tray Wellington Band and with the genre- blurring comedy-grass outfit\, The Cleverlys. \nTogether\, Thomas Cassell & Nick Fallon offer audiences a listening experience that feels at once deeply rooted and refreshingly modern – equal parts intimate and virtuosic – showcasing just how expansive contemporary bluegrass can be. \nCall 707-477-6309 for reservations
URL:https://californiabluegrass.org/event/thomas-cassell-and-nick-at-out-west-garage/
LOCATION:Out West Garage\, 321 Second Street\, Petaluma\, 94952\, United States
CATEGORIES:Concert
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://californiabluegrass.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Cassell_Fallon.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Golocal": "https://golocal.coop/event/cosmos-and-cocoa/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:golocal
X-SOURCE:GoLocal Cooperative
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T220000
DTSTAMP:20260507T065356Z
CREATED:20260507T065356Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260507T065356Z
UID:70387-1789239600-1789250400@golocal.coop
SUMMARY:Cosmos and Cocoa
DESCRIPTION:Begin your evening with a guided hike along our Planet Walk Trail\, a flat and scenic journey to Saturn and back\, approximately 1.2 miles in total\, beneath the darkening sky as knowledgeable docents offer insightful facts at each planetary stop. Did you know: each step in our planet walk is equivalent to 2.3 million miles through our solar system! \nAfter the walk\, return to the Robert Ferguson Observatory to warm up with a cup of hot cocoa and an in-depth stargazing session led by one of our experienced astronomers. The night sky tour blends science and storytelling\, helping you appreciate the night sky in a whole new way. \nOnce the Star guide portion concludes\, guests are welcome to refill their cocoa and continue observing through our telescopes for the remainder of the night. \nThis program is designed for families and guests of all ages who can comfortably enjoy a light hike and remain respectful and attentive while volunteers offer information. Please wear appropriate footwear and bring a white-light flashlight for this event only.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/cosmos-and-cocoa/
LOCATION:Robert Ferguson Observatory\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Road\, Kenwood\, CA
CATEGORIES:Kids and Family,Other,Recreation
END:VEVENT
