SUMMARY:Oak Woodlands Photography and Field Ecology Guided Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T190000
UID:260820f1dlwbFB3E2nmNaex9uuyw
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is a fun and easy hike through Crane Creek Regio
 nal Park\, where you'll be able to explore oak woodlands and oak savannahs
  with a certified California Naturalist and nature photographer. You'll le
 arn some of the most fascinating details about oak woodlands that often go
  unnoticed\, all while learning how to capture the beauty using your camer
 a to its best abilities. This course is beginner-friendly and accessible f
 or all hiking skill levels. Get pro tips and techniques on landscapes\, pl
 ant photography\, or wildlife photography.\n\nThis workshop requires that 
 you own or have access to a camera that is not a phone camera. DSLRs and m
 irrorless SLRs are recommended\, however bridge cameras and high-end point
 -and-shoots can also work well. This workshop is very beginner-friendly- d
 on't worry if you have no idea how to use your camera yet! That's what I'm
  here for.\n\nThe hike will take place late afternoon\, when we have a goo
 d chance of catching some golden hour lighting for landscapse toward the e
 nd. Be aware that there is an $8 day-use fee as it is a regional park.
LOCATION:Crane Creek Regional park
URL:https://www.westerfieldartworks.com/classes#nature-photography
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
