BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://jccsoco.org", "Press Democrat": "http://jccsoco.org"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://jccsoco.org"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Jewish Film Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T183000
UID:260902dMlpQjy2IEmrVvWqj6D4AQ
DESCRIPTION:From an Oscar\, Peabody\, and Emmy award-winning team\, “The
  Stamp Thief” is part detective story\, part heist film\, and part untol
 d history. The documentary investigates a tale dating back to the Holocaus
 t: that a mysterious Nazi stole priceless stamp collections from concentra
 tion camp victims and buried the stolen stamps in a small town in Poland.\
 n\nEmbarking on a real-life “Argo”-like adventure\, one-time “Seinfe
 ld” producer Gary Gilbert sets out to confirm the story and recover the 
 stamps. His tactic: a fake movie shoot. His goal: to return the stamps to 
 their rightful owners\, hopefully delivering a small measure of justice mo
 re than 70 years after the Holocaust.\n\n**\\= FILM FACTS =**\n\n**Running
  Time** 103 min\n\n**Genre** Documentary\n\n**MPAA Rating** Not Rated\n
 \n**Starring** James Felix Cook Laura Putney Betsy Zajko\n\n**Directed by*
 * Dan Sturman
LOCATION:Rialto Cinemas Sebastopol
URL:http://jccsoco.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
