SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T163000
UID:260909mo0AwQAvG06SbFNCVg0Ckw
DESCRIPTION:September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month. On Monday\, 
 Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person Senio
 r Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\, CA.
  The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.-4:3
 0 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming native 
 artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in the
 ir art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts. The
  artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, guest cur
 ator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·  
        Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\, cu
 ltural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry Edwar
 d Frank\, Yurok/Kashaya Pomo\, who will show paintings and work with Legos
  titled Mind Prison\,\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas \\(Nico
 \\) Vargas\, Kashia Band of Pomo Indians\, whose art was featured at the 5
 5th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carretero\; 
 Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\, Kash
 ia Band of Pomo Indians\; Angelica Smith\, Manchester Point Arena and Yoka
 yo Rancheria\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\, Kashia Ba
 nd of Pomo Indians\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaugh\; Katie Wi
 lliams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, Big Valley Pomo Tribe.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.crushersofcomedy.com/sept182026.html", "Press Democrat": "https://www.crushersofcomedy.com/sept182026.html"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.crushersofcomedy.com/sept182026.html"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Laugh Your Pickkleball Off!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T120000
UID:260830IvcROlQCz02Zk9E7CtkiuA
DESCRIPTION:Laugh Your Pickleball Off!™ is more than a pickleball event
 —it's a chance to make a lasting impact—it's a celebration with a purp
 ose! Every registration\, sponsorship\, and donation helps enrich the live
 s of children with autism\, support their families\, and create lasting op
 portunities for growth and connection.\n\nTwo Unforgettable Days:​Septem
 ber 17 & 18\, 2026​ - Third Annual! \n\nThe 2-day event features:\n\n- P
 ickleball clinics with APP World \\#1 pro and two-time USAP National Champ
 ion Jill Braverman\n\n- Play with a Pro exhibition games\n\n- All-levels p
 ickleball Round-robin\n\n-Finale Comedy Show with headliner Shawn Pelofsky
 !\n\n- And more! —all raising funds to support children with autism and 
 their families.\n\nJoin us for an unforgettable night of stand-up comedy f
 eaturing acclaimed comedian\, actress\, writer\, and producer Shawn Pelofs
 ky—a Comedy Store Main Room\, Laugh Factory\, and Hollywood Improv regul
 ar who performs for our troops\, with credits including Community\, Chelse
 a Lately\, and Amazon’s Stretch It Out! Shawn is also a producer on the 
 hit show Funny You Should Ask!\n\nThe indoor Championship Court at Centerl
 ine 33 Pickleball Complex in Rohnert Park—formerly a movie theater—bec
 omes the setting for a one-of-a-kind comedy show\, where the original thea
 ter seats still provide the best seats in the house. Because comedy belong
 s everywhere even on a pickleball court. \n\nWhether you're a pickleball 
 fan\, a comedy lover\, or simply looking for a unique night out\, bring yo
 ur friends and enjoy an evening of laughter for a great cause.
LOCATION:Centerline 33
URL:https://www.crushersofcomedy.com/sept182026.html
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Formative Influence Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T160000
UID:260909y60nxSvXo0CzP1ZpgsccQw
DESCRIPTION:Formative Influence explores the transformative power of light
  across five bodies of work. Inspired by the landscapes of Northern Califo
 rnia and the American West\, the exhibition examines the shift from photog
 raphy\, where light is observed and captured\, to painting\, where light i
 s created to shape new visual experiences. Rather than documenting the lan
 dscape\, these works evoke its emotional resonance\, emphasizing atmospher
 e\, memory\, and perception over literal representation.
LOCATION:Marin Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
