UID:260902Rs3TTiRl0USUF5ArAt5IIw
DESCRIPTION:Featuring more than 90 photographs of gardens and landscapes\,
  explore local author Louise Leff's book as it looks closely at the moment
 s that connect one space to another and the many ways those transitions in
 fluence how we see and experience a garden.\n\n"The spaces between one gar
 den area and another are often overlooked\, yet they can be some of the mo
 st memorable parts of a landscape."\n\nPrepare to explore this beautiful b
 ook\, discuss with landscaping expert Louise Leff\, and enjoy some light r
 efreshments with us.\n\n- Louise Leff
LOCATION:Usher Gallery
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1598342008661995/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.sonomaroses.org"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Join Us For An English Garden Escape!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T200000
UID:260827oZAUCm-u-0SztAq3dZqVow
DESCRIPTION:Take a seat and travel with us through the remarkable gardens 
 of Northern England\, each with its own history\, character\, and unforget
 table beauty.\n\nThrough personal photography and slideshow narration of h
 er recent trip to England\, Barbara Ellis \\(one of our longtime Master Co
 nsulting Rosarians\\) will take us to the grounds of Holker Hall\, Gresgar
 th Hall\, Littlethorpe Manor\, Mottisfont Abbey\, and Coton Manor\, and mo
 re. From grand country estates and celebrated landscapes to intimate garde
 n rooms overflowing with roses and perennial borders\, this program is you
 r virtual ticket across the pond to discover inspired planting combination
 s\, distinctive garden design\, historic roses\, and plenty of ideas to br
 ing home to your own garden.\n\n..........................................
 ..............\n\nThe Historic Gardens Of Northern England\n\nThursday\, S
 eptember 17 at 6:30pm\n\nLuther Burbank Art & Garden Center\n\nFree to att
 end!
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Art & Garden Center
URL:https://www.sonomaroses.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T193000
UID:260415oIEaFkrv7EalmrVMAWZUpA
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
