X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh00000C6cGbMAJ"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Ross Barbieri\, Y8S\, Christina Lovett
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T223000
UID:260909d8CB50FU8kyOIwXo0gSv4w
DESCRIPTION:$15 General Admission\n\nDoors at 7:30pm.\n\nShow from 8:15-10
 :30pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$3 off each ticket when you 
 use the code earlybird11 at checkout. Offer ends September 13th.\n\nPro
 mo Codes are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitiv
 e\, but must be typed as one word.\n\nRooted in Sonoma County\, singer-son
 gwriter Ross Barbieri crafts a modern\, genre-bending evolution of Ameri
 cana. His music balances warm\, inviting vocals with intricate\, dynamical
 ly woven guitar lines. Drawing inspiration from artists like Foy Vance\, M
 adison Cunningham\, and The Barr Brothers\, Barbieri’s songwriting leave
 s space for the listener—painting an unfinished picture where personal e
 xperiences fill in the gaps. He is currently in the studio recording his d
 ebut EP. @rossmakesnoise\n\nY8S is Bay Area musician Isaac Yates. Raised 
 in a musical family and sharpened behind the kit in local bands\, he write
 s from a wide well of influences — Mali blues\, ’90s grunge\, West Coa
 st underground hip-hop — and blends them into something hard to pin down
 : heavy-hitting live drums\, soulful vocals\, and fine-tuned pop productio
 n. New music monthly.\n\nhttps://www.isaacy8s.com\n\nhttps://youtube.com/@
 Y8S?si=oBj4x1yso78EhNkm\n\n@isaacy8s\n\nhttps://facebook.com/isaacsamuelya
 tes\n\nhttps://open.spotify.com/artist/17CrpEf5BHlRwoOub54szS\n\nChristina
  Lovett \n\n@christinalovettmusic
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 0000C6cGbMAJ
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacific/", "Press Democrat": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacific/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacific/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T223000
UID:260803I6vTi20B9EGW4TtKswEzPQ
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
