BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/", "Press Democrat": "https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:macbitches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T210000
UID:260820GI2qM2JGS0WwR_pZ9LuRzA
DESCRIPTION:“macbitches takes Shakespearean themes and grounds them in 
 a recognizable\, modern reality — a smarter\, theater-centered Mean Gir
 ls\, if you will. It’s funny\, sharp\, and unafraid to let women be comp
 licated.” - Jeanette Seisdedos\, director\n\nmacbitches takes a darkly 
 funny look at the toxic\, high-stakes world of university theater\, center
 ing on a freshman who unexpectedly lands the role of Lady Macbeth. The pla
 y centers on freshman acting major Hailey\, who unexpectedly scores the co
 veted role of Lady Macbeth. Her upperclassmen rivals immediately invite he
 r over to “celebrate.” As the Fireball and Svedka flow\, the young wom
 en interrogate their own ambitions as well as the power structures that ha
 ve shaped their education—and when the night spirals into violent and sh
 ocking acts of betrayal\, they come to learn that what’s done cannot be 
 undone.\n\n\\*Content Advisory: Strong profanity\, physical and psycholog
 ical violence\, heavy substance abuse and underage drinking\, discussions 
 of mental illness and sexual misconduct\, and themes of betrayal and suici
 de. Recommended for mature audiences 16+.\n\nWritten by Sophie McIntosh\n\
 nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos\n\nRunning Time: 90 minutes with no interm
 ission\n\nSeptember 4th\, 5th\, 6th\, \\*10th\, 11th\, 12th\, 13th\, 18th\
 , 19th\, 20th.\n\nFriday and Saturday Shows: 7:30 PM\n\nSunday Matinee: 
 2:00 PM\n\n\\*Value Thursday: 7:30 PM\n\n Adults: $25\n\nStudent w/ID:
  $10\n\n\\*Special Value Thursday Performance:  Pay What You Can\n\nWri
 tten by Sophie McIntosh\n\nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://tinyurl.com/fosterpetaluma"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Aaron Foster | "Mostly Jokes" | Stand Up Comedy @ Roosters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T210000
UID:260808g79bUvhuwUGECmOsxM-9pQ
DESCRIPTION:Aaron Foster never imagined that the best way to manage his 
 depression\, anxiety and griedf would be by telling jokes about it\, but h
 is award winning and darkly funny stand-up show "Mostly Jokes" - that one 
 reviewer called "subversively hilarious\, laugh out loud gallows humor" - 
 has helped him\, and others\, find light in very dark places. \n\n"Mostly
  Jokes" : Growing up with a bipolar father and a schizophrenic older broth
 er left Aaron Foster with a combination of survivor’s guilt\, depression
  and anxiety that has invalidated his every accomplishment\, destroyed his
  every relationship and invaded his every waking thought. A comedy! \n\nF
 irst performed at the Hollywood Fringe Festival to reviews such as: "Some 
 shows claim to be dark humor\, but this was the absolute epitome of it." "
 You will fall in love with a man who would rather you not." "A laugh every
  20 seconds." \n\nFoster is the former host of HGTV’s FreeStyle and has
  performed in theaters and comedy clubs around the country. A few of his m
 ain influences are Mike Birbiglia\, Maria Bamford\, Gary Gulman\, Marc Mar
 on\, Taylor Tomlinson and Neal Brennan. Do with that information what you 
 will.
LOCATION:Polly Klaas Theater
URL:http://tinyurl.com/fosterpetaluma
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacific/", "Press Democrat": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacific/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacific/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T223000
UID:260803pUepRGtGV0e6QcviLceskQ
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
