SUMMARY:Salsa Beginner Marin – Saturday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T110000
UID:260317RjCJzhwAIEmfiFhmXkPJyg
DESCRIPTION:**Ready to learn intermediate steps and technique?** Join on 
 on Saturday – Salsa Beginner Marin\n\nAre you a beginner who’s always 
 wanted to learn salsa? Salsa classes are designed to help you build a stro
 ng foundation. In this class\, you’ll learn the fundamental footwork\, p
 ractice the basic turns\, and understand the essential body movement that 
 will make you feel confident on the dance floor. This class is perfect for
  anyone ready to learn the techniques and foundational steps needed to sta
 rt their salsa journey.\n\nSalsa is fun\, and we make learning it stress-f
 ree! Our relaxed\, beginner-friendly class is the ideal starting point. Yo
 u don’t need a partner\, nor any dance experience!\n\nIn this class you 
 will learn:\n\nBasic directional steps that form the foundation of salsa.\
 n\nProper frame for comfortable and effective partner-work.\n\nSimple\, ea
 sy-to-remember turn patterns.\n\nGet ready to learn the fundamentals and h
 ave a great time!\n\n**Details:**\n\n**No partner necessary**—rotations 
 ensure everyone dances\n\nPlease wear **non-marking shoes** to protect t
 he floor\n\nArrive 10 minutes early\; warm up and settle in\n\n**When:** 
 Saturday\, 10:00 am – 11:00 am\n\n**Where:** 4140 Redwood Highway #8\, 
 San Rafael\, CA
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8\, San Rafael\, CA
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-beginners-saturday/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.cmosc.org/event/cuentos-con-ritmo-stories-with-rhythm-8-copy/2026-09-19/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Cuentos con Ritmo (Stories with Rhythm)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T103000
UID:260912KN4BzNvAHU-BKx19cNPLOQ
DESCRIPTION:Cuentos con Ritmo \\(Stories with Rhythm\\)\n\n\n\nCuentos con
  Ritmo | Cuentos \\* Música \\* Movimiento \n\nPresentado por Colors of S
 panish \n\nCuentos con Ritmo es una oportunidad única semanal para niños
  de 1 a 5 años y sus familias\, el cual aporta alegría\, comprensión y 
 aprecio por la lengua española a toda la comunidad. Durante Cuentos con R
 itmo\, los pequeños visitantes y sus familias participan de forma lúdica
  en historias interactivas con música y movimiento fortaleciendo nuestra 
 diversa comunidad y entusiasmo por la lengua meta. \n\nCuentos con Ritmo e
 s presentado por Guadalupe Tausch en colaboración con la organización qu
 e fundó\, Colors of Spanish. Originaria del estado de Guanajuato en Méxi
 co\, tiene una maestría en español con énfasis en la adquisición de un
 a segunda lengua para la primera infancia y continúa sus estudios enfocad
 a en la primera infancia especializándose en la adquisición de idiomas a
  través de la música/movimiento. Colors of Spanish ofrece talleres para 
 profesores\, bibliotecarios y cuidadores y organiza programas de cuentos e
 n español con música y movimiento en escuelas\, bibliotecas y museos loc
 ales. www.colorsofspanish.org \n\nCuentos con Ritmo | Cuentos \\* Música 
 \\* Movimiento \n\nPresented by Colors of Spanish \n\nCuentos con Ritmo \\
 (Stories with Rhythm\\) is a weekly one-of-a-kind opportunity for children
  ages 1-5 and their families that brings joy\, understanding and appreciat
 ion for the Spanish language to Spanish- and English-speaking speakers ali
 ke. During Cuentos con Ritmo\, young visitors and their families playfully
  engage in interactive stories with music and movement that build communit
 y and an excitement for language! \n\nCuentos con Ritmo is presented by Gu
 adalupe Tausch in collaboration with the organization she founded\, Colors
  of Spanish. Originally from the state of Guanajuato in México\, she has 
 a master’s degree in Spanish with emphasis in second language acquisitio
 n for early childhood and continues her study of childhood and music/movem
 ent trainings. Colors of Spanish provides workshops for teachers\, librari
 ans and caregivers and hosts Spanish story time with music & movement prog
 rams at local schools\, libraries\, and museums. www.colorsofspanish.org \
 n\nDesigned for kids 1-5\, families\, and siblings. \n\n \n\nGenerously sp
 onsored by RCU and the SABA Foundation.
LOCATION:Children's Museum of Sonoma County
URL:https://www.cmosc.org/event/cuentos-con-ritmo-stories-with-rhythm-8-co
 py/2026-09-19/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/workshop-platen-press-fundamentals/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Workshop: Platen Press Fundamentals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T150000
UID:260713FhmQfKvD4UqUi8CH00rjjQ
DESCRIPTION:PLATEN PRESS FUNDAMENTALS Master the platen press by designing
  and printing your own edition of letterpress greeting cards. This worksho
 p focuses on the specific techniques and rhythm of platen press operation-
 feeding paper\, achieving even impression\, and producing clean\, consiste
 nt prints. You'll set metal type to create one card design\, then print an
  edition of 15 cards to take home. Through hands-on practice\, you'll lear
 n makeready\, lockup\, ink coverage\, and troubleshooting common press iss
 ues. By the end of the workshop\, you'll understand how to operate a plate
 n press confidently and have beautiful cards ready to send or gift. Ideal 
 for printers who want to add platen press skills to their repertoire and c
 reate functional\, finished work. third saturdays\\* 10:00am - 3:00pm \\*n
 o class in November
