X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.scgsonline.org"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Researching School-Related Records of Our Ancestors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T143000
UID:260909P2PFOZ1wi0iZSfGs_lFntw
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society Presents\n\n Researchi
 ng School-Related Records of Our Ancestors\n\n with Lisa S. Gorrell\, CG®
 \n\n Locating our ancestors’ school records can give us a glimpse into 
 their early life. Records can be in family papers\, archives\, and online.
  This presentation will consider public and religious schools\, vocational
  schools\, and colleges.\n\n Lisa S. Gorrell is a Certified Genealogist®
 . She has served on boards of several genealogical societies and is curren
 tly the recording secretary with the Contra Costa County Historical Societ
 y\, where she volunteers at their archives. She enjoys giving genealogy pr
 esentations and writing about her family on two blogs: “Mam-ma’s South
 ern Family”\n\nhttp://mam-massouthernfamily.blogspot.com/ and “My Trai
 ls into the Past” http://mytrailsintothepast.blogspot.com/. She has writ
 ten a three-generation family history about her husband’s Swedish ancest
 ors.\n\n Saturday\, September 19th\n\n Meeting starts at 12:30 pm\, pres
 entation starts at 1:00 pm PST\n\n Meeting Details : The meeting is held 
 via Zoom. Login begins at 12:30 p.m.\n\n FREE Via ZOOM\n\nRegister at ht
 tps://www.scgsonline.org\n\n Registration closes Friday\, September 18th
URL:https://www.scgsonline.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
