UID:2609090F6t9IM-akKqMg8nGyHPrg
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to play chess and practice your skills with the Blac
 k Men's Chess League! This two-hour program will consist of a semi-formal 
 instructional section\, followed by an open session where participants can
  play with others. This program is for kids ages 5-18\, any background or 
 experience is welcome. Playing materials and snacks will be provided. The 
 Black Men's Chess league is a Bay Area based non-profit created by black m
 en dedicated to teaching and fostering community. \\*Registration is requi
 red\\*  CLICK HERE TO REGISTER
LOCATION:Springstowne Library
URL:https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/17283375
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
