CREATED:20260820T205802Z
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma County DSA\, Indivisible\, Working Family Parties\, and 
 the North bay Labor Council Present: Doorstep Democracy\nSpend a day learni
 ng how to make the biggest impact on elections. This Conference will give y
 ou new skills and confidence to knock on doors\, talk to your neighbors\, a
 nd help elect progressives that will change the balance of power in this co
 unty in November. No prior experience? No problem! Door knocked before? You
 're in the right place. We need to turn out the people who want to make Son
 oma County work for all of us\, not just the big-monied interests.\nWorksho
 ps on canvassing\, phone banking and texting for political campaigns. After
  lunch\, we'll all go out an canvas for Joana Paun and Melanie Bagby then w
 e'll come back and debrief!\nREGISTER for this Free TrainingGreat for all e
 xperience levels!tinyurl.com/4sw7bpbb\nNote: You may RSVP on this page to e
 nable text/email updates from us\, but please also RSVP at the link above!\
 n\nRSVP: https://solidarity.socodsa.org/workshop-training-doorstep-democrac
