X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/a-beginners-guide-to-writing-your-first-book-tickets-1998672151207", "Press Democrat": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/a-beginners-guide-to-writing-your-first-book-tickets-1998672151207"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/a-beginners-guide-to-writing-your-first-book-tickets-1998672151207"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:A Beginners Guide to Writing Your First Book
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T110000
UID:260912UGHsOeVuHUCJAZeA_8iVEw
DESCRIPTION:A Beginners Guide to Writing Your First Book\n\nReady to start
  your writing journey? Join us online for fun\, easy-to-follow tips that w
 ill help you craft your very first book. Whether you’ve got a story brew
 ing or just the idea\, this event is perfect to kickstart your writing adv
 enture. Get inspired\, learn the basics\, and connect with fellow newbie w
 riters—all from the comfort of your home!\n\nThe work is there. And it
 ’s still sitting in a drawer\, a hard drive\, a notebook that never quit
 e becomes the thing it was supposed to be. Or worse\, it’s stuck in your
  head\, because you haven’t found the courage to put something on that b
 lank page.\n\nOuch\, I know. But that’s where we all have to start.\n\nT
 here are three things that keep most writers and authors stuck: overthinki
 ng\, fear of rejection\, and obscurity.\n\nI can help you with all three.\
 n\nIn this workshop\, we’ll get past the blank page together. You’ll l
 eave with a real starting habit\, not just inspiration.\n\nI have a goal o
 n my calendar every day that I follow 90% of the time: write for one hour\
 , or 500 words. It works. I’ve published seven books\, with dozens more 
 outlined.\n\nOnce you start\, magic happens. We write the first word\, the
 n a sentence\, then a paragraph\, and soon\, if we stick with it\, we have
  what Anne Lamott famously called a “shitty first draft.”\n\nThat’s 
 not a bad thing. That’s the thing.\n\nDon’t let the process get in the
  way of productivity. That’s just another form of procrastination.\n\nFR
 EE GUIDE!\n\nEvery attendee gets a link to From Here to There\, my free pl
 anning guide for closing your mindset gaps without sacrificing your soul.\
 n\nWant to learn more?\n\nVisit: shawnlangwell.com
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/a-beginners-guide-to-writing-your-first-b
