BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.artescapesonoma.com/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.artescapesonoma.com/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.artescapesonoma.com/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Ceramic Carving - Mini Ofrenda Bowls
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T150000
UID:260808ZcLpd1bQWkaYOC4TVpF3Ng
DESCRIPTION:Join Kelly from No Peach Ceramics for this special ceramic car
 ving class. \n\nHand carve a set of mini ofrenda bowls for your home alta
 r! Each participant will receive 4–6 handmade bowls to personalize using
  simple carving techniques and colorful glazes.\n\nSgraffito is an ancient
  technique of surface decoration that involves scratching or carving throu
 gh a layer to reveal a contrasting color beneath. During the course of thi
 s 3-hour workshop\, we will cover the fundamentals of which tools and tech
 niques to best apply \\(and then remove\\) slips and underglazes to a pre-
 prepared clay "canvas". Demonstrations of when and how to carve successful
 ly will be supplemented with in-depth advice on each aspect of the sgraffi
 to process. \n\n All experience levels are welcome! You will be provided
  with materials\, tools\, and forms to practice sgraffito and make your ow
 n unique platter. Bringing inspiration photos and design ideas is welcomed
  and encouraged! We will be providing one pre-prepared raw clay platter pe
 r student to use during the course. After the class\, we will fire your fi
 nished piece\, and it will be ready for pickup within 2-3 weeks.
LOCATION:Art Escape
URL:https://www.artescapesonoma.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://linktr.ee/INeedAMic"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:I Need a Mic: Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
UID:260815f-5SiTxF9UaGDWVw_tGbuw
DESCRIPTION:Welcome poets\, writers\, and artists of Vallejo. My name is R
 ay\, and I am your host of I NEED A MIC OPEN MIC.\n\nThis is more than jus
 t a stage — it’s a space. A space where voices rise\, stories breathe\
 , and truth finds its rhythm. \n\nWhether you carry poems in your chest\,
  songs in your spirit\, or stories that have been waiting for the right mo
 ment — this is your invitation.\n\nWe gather not just to perform\, but t
 o connect. To celebrate the raw\, the real\, and the unapologetically huma
 n art of expression. Every voice matters here. Every perspective adds to t
 he pulse of this room.\n\nBut understand — this is a space built on resp
 ect. While we welcome passion\, depth\, and honesty\, we do not tolerate h
 ate\, disrespect\, or harmful rhetoric. Heavy political agendas that divid
 e rather than inspire have no place here. \n\nThis stage is for expressio
 n\, not oppression.\n\nBring your truth. Bring your courage. Bring your ar
 t.\n\nCome share. Come listen. Come feel something.\n\nBecause someone in 
 that room might need exactly what you have to say.\n\nI NEED A MIC — and
  maybe\, so do you.
LOCATION:City Arts Gallery
URL:https://linktr.ee/INeedAMic
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
