SUMMARY:Los Farmerz & Los Huracanes del Norte
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
UID:260910OkGApyB3EUiYMjAKXgNTCA
DESCRIPTION:Throughout a remarkable career that has spanned more than four
  decades\, Los Huracanes del Norte have established themselves as one of t
 he most popular Norteño groups in the genre\, a reputation that has allow
 ed them to tour extensively and build a global fanbase. Whether mingling w
 ith industry representatives at an awards show or delighting ticket buyers
  during a high-energy performance that accompanies a rodeo\, Los Huracanes
  del Norte have had no trouble demonstrating why they've been able to sust
 ain such a lengthy and prosperous career. Live shows are particularly memo
 rable and feature rousing musical arrangements that accompany signature ha
 rmonies. Their discography includes dozens of albums\, including the most 
 recent\, "Como Un Huracán\," released in 2012. \n\nAlthough the band form
 ed in 1969 under the name Los Cuatro del Norte\, their breakthrough didn't
  come until almost a decade later\, in 1978\, when "La Musiquera" went on 
 to become their first album to sell hundreds of thousands of copies. For t
 he next decade and a half\, the band consistently ranked in the top ten of
  Billboard's regional Mexican charts. In 2002\, 2009 and 2011\, the band w
 as nominated at the Latin Grammy Awards for Best Norteño Album. That show
 s how even concert attendees know to expect memorable performances from th
 e group\, the music industry at large similarly recognizes the artistic me
 rit evident in Los Huracanes del Norte's studio efforts. The band's perpet
 ual success on the charts and their ability to draw concert crowds is a te
 stament to loyalty and appreciation from Norteño fans who hail from numer
 ous regions of the world.
LOCATION:RODEO SANTA FE
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039845484?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/", "Press Democrat": "https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Bye Bye Birdie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T160000
UID:2609106uzQE0cQpEmdks3-8t1Jgw
DESCRIPTION:A joyful\, high-energy musical comedy packed with unforgettabl
 e songs\, humor\, and heart\, "Bye Bye Birdie" is a celebration of youth\,
  fame\, and the delightful chaos that happens when pop culture collides wi
 th small-town life.\n\nFrom the high-energy “The Telephone Hour” to th
 e show-stopping “A Lot of Livin’ to Do\,” the heartfelt “How Lovel
 y to Be a Woman\,” and the iconic “Put On a Happy Face\,” this produ
 ction is filled with classic musical theater moments the whole family can 
 enjoy.\n\nCinnabar Theater's production is directed by Zachary Hasbany\, w
 ith book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, and lyrics by Lee
  Adams\, originally produced by Edward Padula. The show is presented throu
 gh special arrangement with Concord Theatricals.\n\nShow details\n\nCreate
 d by: Book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, lyrics by Lee A
 dams\n\nDirector: Zachary Hasbany\n\nLocation: Sonoma State University –
  Warren Theater\, Ives Hall\, 1801 East Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA 949
 28\n\nPerformance dates: September 18 – October 4\, 2026\; Fridays & Sat
 urdays 7:30pm\, Sundays 2:00pm\n\nEstimated run time: 2 hours\, with one 1
 0-minute intermission\n\nRecommended for families / all ages\n\nASL-Interp
 reted Performance\n\nSunday\, September 27 at 2:00 PM\n\nThis performance 
 will feature American Sign Language \\(ASL\\) interpretation. Patrons who 
 would like seating with a clear view of the ASL interpreter can contact th
 e Box Office at \\(707\\) 763-8920 or boxoffice@cinnabartheater.org.\n\nTi
 ckets: https://ci.ovationtix.com/35211
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Auditorium
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
