BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://events.humanitix.com/peace-fest-2026", "Press Democrat": "https://events.humanitix.com/peace-fest-2026"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://events.humanitix.com/peace-fest-2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:San Geronimo Valley Community Center's Peace Fest : Art and Music 
 Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T180000
UID:2608317Rh1QlYobkO5ObK3gZOuRw
DESCRIPTION:The Sunday afternoon of Peace Fest celebrates creativity\, com
 munity\, and the ways music and art can inspire peace and human connection
 .\n\nThe festivities begin at 2 p.m. with a ceremonial blessing by Henr
 y Frank\, whose wisdom and presence have become a treasured Peace Fest tra
 dition. Visitors can also experience Henry Frank: A Human Experience in t
 he West Room\, while the Valley Room will feature artwork from the Willia
 m James Association's Prison Arts Project.\n\nOutside\, students from Lag
 unitas School will exhibit peace-inspired artwork created following Ashan
 ti Branch's Taking Off the Mask workshop. Through interactive activities 
 and thoughtful conversation\, students explore identity\, empathy\, and au
 thentic connection\, expressing both their inner and outer selves through 
 art. Also\, outside near the Courtyard the GreenStitch Climate Action in
 terns will once again create one of their vibrant community chalk murals\,
  illustrating the connection between climate protection and world peace.\n
 \nFollowing the blessing\, we are excited to present all the way from Para
 quay\, Orquestra de Reciclados de Cateura\, an internationally acclaimed 
 youth ensemble from Paraguay whose musicians perform on instruments handcr
 afted from recycled materials recovered from a landfill. The instruments p
 layed by the orchestra members mimic violins\, violas\, cellos\, double ba
 sses\, guitars\, flutes\, saxophones\, trumpets\, trombones\, and percussi
 on instruments\, yet they are constructed from refuse. Their repertoire in
 cludes classical\, folk\, Paraguayan\, and Latin American music\, as well 
 as songs by the Beatles and Frank Sinatra\, among others. Their inspiring 
 story of resilience\, creativity\, and hope beautifully reflects the spiri
 t of Peace Fest.\n\nPeace Fest will then welcome Enriching Lives Through M
 usic \\(ELM\\) for the first time. The youth music education program provi
 des young people with immersive musical experiences\, mentorship\, and the
  resources to pursue their artistic dreams. Their talented young performer
 s promise to bring energy\, enthusiasm\, and inspiration to the afternoon.
 \n\nClosing this year's festival is featured headliner AgapéSoul\, led b
 y bassist\, songwriter\, and producer Darryl Anders.Blending soul\, funk\
 , jazz\, and R&B\, AgapéSoul delivers uplifting performances centered on 
 hope\, healing\, and connection. Anders has performed with the legendary T
 ower of Power and toured and recorded with Meters drummer Zigaboo Modelist
 e\, bringing decades of musical experience to the Peace Fest stage.\n\nAs 
 Anders describes it\, "The name AgapéSoul comes from the Greek word Agape
 —meaning God's unconditional love—and Soul\, the place within us where
  music comes from. It also reflects the style of music I feel connected to
 . As an artist\, I feel it's important to speak on issues that are crucial
  to the healing of our society."
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://events.humanitix.com/peace-fest-2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/", "Press Democrat": "https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:macbitches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T153000
UID:2608201vd-hRgPmEmMTVAmcUTSMA
DESCRIPTION:“macbitches takes Shakespearean themes and grounds them in 
 a recognizable\, modern reality — a smarter\, theater-centered Mean Gir
 ls\, if you will. It’s funny\, sharp\, and unafraid to let women be comp
 licated.” - Jeanette Seisdedos\, director\n\nmacbitches takes a darkly 
 funny look at the toxic\, high-stakes world of university theater\, center
 ing on a freshman who unexpectedly lands the role of Lady Macbeth. The pla
 y centers on freshman acting major Hailey\, who unexpectedly scores the co
 veted role of Lady Macbeth. Her upperclassmen rivals immediately invite he
 r over to “celebrate.” As the Fireball and Svedka flow\, the young wom
 en interrogate their own ambitions as well as the power structures that ha
 ve shaped their education—and when the night spirals into violent and sh
 ocking acts of betrayal\, they come to learn that what’s done cannot be 
 undone.\n\n\\*Content Advisory: Strong profanity\, physical and psycholog
 ical violence\, heavy substance abuse and underage drinking\, discussions 
 of mental illness and sexual misconduct\, and themes of betrayal and suici
 de. Recommended for mature audiences 16+.\n\nWritten by Sophie McIntosh\n\
 nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos\n\nRunning Time: 90 minutes with no interm
 ission\n\nSeptember 4th\, 5th\, 6th\, \\*10th\, 11th\, 12th\, 13th\, 18th\
 , 19th\, 20th.\n\nFriday and Saturday Shows: 7:30 PM\n\nSunday Matinee: 
 2:00 PM\n\n\\*Value Thursday: 7:30 PM\n\n Adults: $25\n\nStudent w/ID:
  $10\n\n\\*Special Value Thursday Performance:  Pay What You Can\n\nWri
 tten by Sophie McIntosh\n\nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
