SUMMARY:Mickelson Pumpkin Patch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T090000
UID:260906PWXOUdZYDEuCRtGALaT3lA
DESCRIPTION:Mickelson Pumpkin Patch\, just past the Marin-Sonoma county li
 ne off Highway 101\, offers a wide variety of pumpkins\, squash\, and gour
 ds as well as activities like a hay maze and pyramid\, tractor rides\, pai
 ntball gallery\, birthday parties and more. They also have food vendors an
 d even craft beer available. No outside food or dogs allowed. Admission: M
 onday - Friday: FREE! Saturdays & Sundays: $5 Per Person additional charge
  for specific activities \\(  find out more here \\) Directions: To get th
 ere\, take Highway 101 north to the Petaluma Boulevard South/Kastania Road
  exit \\(Exit 472A\\). Turn right at the stoplight then turn right onto Pe
 taluma Boulevard South. Follow the road south until you get to the pumpkin
  patch\, which will be on your left.
LOCATION:Mickelson Pumpkin Patch
URL:https://www.marinmommies.com/calendar/mickelson-pumpkin-patch-2
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Formative Influence Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T160000
UID:260909KArTGUTDuE22dZIO4watEQ
DESCRIPTION:Formative Influence explores the transformative power of light
  across five bodies of work. Inspired by the landscapes of Northern Califo
 rnia and the American West\, the exhibition examines the shift from photog
 raphy\, where light is observed and captured\, to painting\, where light i
 s created to shape new visual experiences. Rather than documenting the lan
 dscape\, these works evoke its emotional resonance\, emphasizing atmospher
 e\, memory\, and perception over literal representation.
LOCATION:Marin Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
