BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/intermediate-salsa-class/17159571/2026-09-22T18", "Press Democrat": "https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-class-intermediate-tuesday/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/intermediate-salsa-class/17159571/2026-09-22T18"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T193000
UID:260704IBeUMYSCkU-lEnRrS_6yBQ
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 6:30PM – 7:30PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/intermediate-salsa-clas
 s/17159571/2026-09-22T18
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108736158?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Tyler Reeve & Django Walker
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T190000
UID:260910nrA5nl7PWkCFIqvviiMQ-w
DESCRIPTION:Born in Mobile\, Alabama\, and educated \\(socially at the ver
 y least\\) at The Florida State University\, Tyler’s down home sensibili
 ty\, attitude and humor come across in his songs and through his live perf
 ormances.  Always a storyteller\, songwriting fits quite naturally for Ree
 ve.  “I’m a song guy\; I love songs\, I love stories\, I love the ride
  music can take you on.”  Tyler’s performance are riddled with stories
  – usually funny stories – about inspiration for his songs\, having a 
 few too many\, and even spending a night or two in jail.  \n\n	Reeve has h
 ad his hand in writing some of country music’s biggest songs of the last
  few years\, including the 2018 BMI Song of The Year\, “In Case You Didn
 ’t Know” \\(Brett Young\\)\, which has streamed over 1 Billion times. 
 He also had a multi-week \\#1 & XM The Highway’s 2020 Song of The Year\,
  and ACM Musical Event of The Year nom\, “Does To Me” \\(Luke Combs fe
 aturing Eric Church\\)\, and recent Highway \\#1 Mississippi Or Me \\(Rile
 y Green\\).  Other notables include “Whiskey On My Breath” \\(Love & T
 heft\\)\, “Where I Go When I Drink” \\(Chris Young\\)\, White Girls\, 
 White Wine & Adderall \\(Kid Rock\\)\, How Ya Doin Up There \\(Scotty McCr
 eery\\) and “I Got Away With You” \\(Luke Combs\\).
LOCATION:Carneros Resort and Spa
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108736158?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
