X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://raventheater.org/events/usaf-commanders-jazz-ensemble/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:USAF Commanders Jazz Ensemble
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T193000
UID:260909e5g0dsCFPUmSiu6v0Iutqw
DESCRIPTION:**Free admission\, but ticket required**. Maximum 4 per person
 .\n\nThe ensemble is part of the **United States Air Force Band of the Gol
 den West**\, stationed in the San Francisco Bay Area at Travis Air Force B
 ase\, California. The only active duty Air Force band west of the Rockies\
 , the Band of the Golden West is comprised of about 60 talented and versat
 ile Airmen-musicians under the command of Captain Brian O’Donnell. While
  they honor legends like Duke Ellington\, Count Basie\, and Glenn Miller\,
  they seamlessly transition into cool jazz\, bebop\, Latin rhythms\, Broad
 way hits\, and patriotic music. In addition to performing for civilian com
 munities throughout the states of California\, Washington\, Oregon\, Arizo
 na\, and Nevada\, the band supports 13 Air Force Bases\, 8 Air Force Reser
 ve Wings\, and 6 recruiting squadrons in over 250 annual performances for 
 1.5 million listeners.\n\nThe organization offers several outstanding perf
 orming groups: Concert Band\, Ceremonial Marching Band\, Commanders Jazz E
 nsemble\, Mobility popular music ensemble\, Travis Brass quintet\, Golden 
 West Brass ensemble\, Golden West Winds woodwind quintet\, Sierra Winds wo
 odwind ensemble\, Clarinet Quartet\, and Galaxy popular music ensemble. Ad
 ditionally\, the Band of the Golden West provides solo vocalists for the p
 erformance of our National Anthem and solo buglers for Taps details.\n\nTh
 e Band of the Golden West has performed for gubernatorial inaugurations\, 
 with guest artists such as Marvin Stamm\, Arturo Sandoval and Bob Hope\, a
 nd for the fans of Oakland Athletics\, San Francisco Giants\, Oakland Raid
 ers\, San Francisco 49ers\, and Infineon NASCAR races. In the last ten yea
 rs the band has led off three Tournament of Roses parades in Pasadena\, CA
 . In 2004\, the USAF Band of the Golden West was honored to support the in
 terment ceremony of President Ronald Reagan in Simi Valley\, CA\, an event
 \, viewed by a global TV audience of over 400 million. More recent events 
 include featured performances with the Los Angeles Philharmonic\, San Fran
 cisco Symphony\, the Hollywood Bowl Orchestra and Pentatonix.\n\n**With gr
 atitude to our sponsor\, Eddinger Enterprises\, Inc.**\n\n**Tuesday\, Sept
 ember 22nd\, at 7:30 PM.** Doors open at 6:30 PM.\n\n**Please email us if 
 you need wheelchair accessible spaces so we can reserve it: events@raventh
 eater.org. For people using walkers\, the back row is most suitable as it 
 has more leg room.**
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/usaf-commanders-jazz-ensemble/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
