X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://wl.eventim.us/event/carsie-blanton/697898?afflky=MysticTheatre", "Press Democrat": "https://wl.eventim.us/event/carsie-blanton/697898?afflky=MysticTheatre"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://wl.eventim.us/event/carsie-blanton/697898?afflky=MysticTheatre"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Carsie Blanton with The Burning Hell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260923T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260923T000000
UID:260715lQOokxvsr0yu_Zk7iCA-Zw
DESCRIPTION:**CARSIE BLANTON**\n\nwith support from The Burning Hell\n\n**
 BIOS:**\n\nCarsie Blanton:\n\nCarsie Blanton is a songwriter with hooks\, 
 chutzpah\, and revolutionary optimism. A\n\nradical folk artist in the tra
 dition of Woody Guthrie\, her infectious melodies and lyrical\n\nwit keep 
 listeners rapt while she conjures spirits of vaudeville\, campfire singalo
 ngs\, and\n\npunk rock. Blanton and her road-tested band deploy humor\, ca
 maraderie\, and\n\nconsiderable musical muscle to enroll each audience in 
 a rare vision of hope and\n\nsolidarity.\n\nIn addition to writing and per
 forming music\, Carsie works as a political organizer and\n\nactivist. In 
 fall of 2025\, she participated in the Global Sumud Flotilla\, a direct ac
 tion to\n\nbring humanitarian aid to Gaza by sailboat. In early October\, 
 after a month at sea\, she\n\nwas imprisoned in Israel for five days along
  with hundreds of her comrades.\n\nSoon after\, Blanton released The Littl
 e Flame\, a song of solidarity covered widely on\n\nsocial media during he
 r detention. The Little Flame features background vocals from\n\nIrish ban
 d Ye Vagabonds and Carsie’s Palestinian/New Zealander prison-mate Rana\n
 \nHamida\, and appears on her latest album\, The Red Album Vol II.\n\nAfte
 r two decades spent on the road\, Blanton has amassed a dedicated fan base
  and a small menagerie of viral hits\, and regularly sells out mid-size ve
 nues across the U.S. and Europe. 2026 will find her touring heavily with h
 er own band and in collaboration with Canadian folk-punk rabblerousers The
  Burning Hell\, as well as continuing her organizing work with Artists Aga
 inst Apartheid and the Party for Socialism and Liberation.\n\nThe Burning 
 Hell:\n\nThe Burning Hell is the musical project of songwriter Mathias Kom
  and multi-instrumentalist Ariel Sharratt. Their narrative-driven songs ar
 e packed with literary\, historical\, and pop-cultural subjects\, incorpor
 ating a frequent fixation on apocalypse and ruin into work that celebrates
  participation in a surprising\, wry\, and even occasionally beautiful wor
 ld. Based in the woods of Prince Edward Island\, Canada\, The Burning Hell
  emphasizes connection and commitment to the political power of sharing mu
 sic.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://wl.eventim.us/event/carsie-blanton/697898?afflky=MysticTheatre
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
