BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Livewhale": "https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23756-tom-chown-46-years-behind-the-lens"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:Tom Chown: 46 Years Behind the Lens
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTSTAMP:20260825T094142Z
UID:20260924T070000Z-23756@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20260924
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,3200,3200/688_cs_-_ongoing_Tom_Chown_Photo_Exhibit.r
 ev.1787675576.jpg
CATEGORIES:Arts
DESCRIPTION:Santa Rosa Junior College will celebrate the 46-year career of
  longtime staff photographer Tom Chown with a photography exhibition featu
 ring images from his decades at the college\, from the days of film and da
 rkrooms to the digital era.  Chown began his career at SRJC at age 24\, wo
 rking in the campus photography lab. Over the next 46 years\, he became a 
 familiar presence throughout the college community\, documenting the peopl
 e\, programs and milestones that shaped generations of students and employ
 ees.  The exhibition will trace Chown's evolution as a photographer\, from
  working with film and developing photographs in the darkroom to embracing
  digital photography. It also offers a visual history of SRJC\, preserving
  moments from nearly five decades of college life.  The exhibition is free
  and open to the public.Location: Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery\, Doyle Li
 brary 1st floor - Santa Rosa CampusFor more information\, visit SRJC's Rob
 ert F. Agrella Art Gallery website. (https://art-gallery.santarosa.edu/exh
 ibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-work)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260825T165455Z
LOCATION:Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23756-tom-chown-46-years-behind-t
 he-lens
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Santa Rosa Junior College will celebrate
  the 46-year career of longtime staff photographer Tom Chown with a photog
 raphy exhibition featuring images from his decades at the college\, from t
 he days of film and darkrooms to the digital era.</p><p>  Chown began his 
 career at SRJC at age 24\, working in the campus photography lab. Over the
  next 46 years\, he became a familiar presence throughout the college comm
 unity\, documenting the people\, programs and milestones that shaped gener
 ations of students and employees.</p><p>  The exhibition will trace Chown'
 s evolution as a photographer\, from working with film and developing phot
 ographs in the darkroom to embracing digital photography. It also offers a
  visual history of SRJC\, preserving moments from nearly five decades of c
 ollege life.</p><p>  The exhibition is free and open to the public.</p><p>
 <strong>Location:</strong> Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery\, Doyle Library 1
 st floor - Santa Rosa Campus</p><p><a href="https://art-gallery.santarosa.
 edu/exhibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-work" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For
  more information\, visit SRJC's Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery website.</a
 ></p>
