SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T170000
UID:260910sM5TieGdqkiAA58bIxaUcQ
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Hotel Healdsburg
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108742825?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/in-conversation-sept2026", "Press Democrat": "https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/in-conversation-sept2026"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/in-conversation-sept2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Between Two Plantsmen: Sean Hogan in Conversation with Jim Salyard
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T190000
UID:260905R-AsUCGym0i2wC37YefY7g
DESCRIPTION:What can a lifetime with plants teach us?\n\nJoin Sean Hogan\,
  founder of Cistus Nursery and Gardens\, and Jim Salyards\, Associate Dire
 ctor of Garden Experience at Filoli\, for an intimate conversation at West
 ern Hills Garden.\n\nLong-time friends and fellow plantsmen\, Sean and Jim
  will reflect on horticulture\, legacy gardens\, plant exploration\, and t
 he enduring relationships between people and place.\n\nExpect an evening o
 f stories\, insights\, and thoughtful conversation for gardeners\, horticu
 lturalists\, and anyone who loves the natural world.\n\nThis talk is part 
 of Western Hills Garden’s Horticultural Exchange Series\, bringing toget
 her leading voices in horticulture for thoughtful public conversations.\n\
 nSpeaker Bios:\n\nSean Hogan: Sean is an acclaimed horticulturist\, garden
  consultant\, speaker\, and international plant collector. Convinced to be
 come California’s first certified arborist by Western Hills Garden found
 er Marshall Olbrich\, Sean has had a storied career as a Curator at the Un
 iversity of California Botanical Garden at Berkeley\, and in 1996 he and h
 is partner Parker founded Cistus Design Nursery on Sauvie Island in Oregon
 . Sean is a Founding Board Member of the new Portland Botanical Garden and
  a member of the WHG Horticultural Advisory Committee.\n\nJim Salyards: Ji
 m has worked at Filoli for 30 years\, moving into his current role as Asso
 ciate Director of Garden Experience in early 2025. Jim oversees a wide ran
 ge of programs that support Filoli’s external relations\, learning and e
 ngagement\, development\, retail\, and interpretive strategies\, with a pa
 rticular emphasis on community engagement. He also oversees Filoli’s pla
 nt collections work and is responsible for building and nurturing relation
 ships within the fields of public gardens\, horticultural science\, garden
 ing\, retail product production\, and the culinary arts.
LOCATION:Western Hills Garden
URL:https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/in-conversation-sept2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
