BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/acorn-choir-the-earth-says"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Acorn MusEcology Project: The Earth Says
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T203000
UID:6a87304f933ba062c228e64d@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Acorn MusEcology Project is proud to present the Northern Cali
 fornia premiere of Alex Berko's\nSacred Place\n\, an immersive exploration
  of ecological spirituality set to the words of Wendell Berry\, John Muir\
 , William Stafford\, and Rabindranath Tagore. Acorn's 27-voice ensemble wi
 ll be joined by violin\, cello\, and piano to offer up this song cycle of 
 reverential texts within a richly-layered soundscape. Additional original 
 music by co-directors Sarah Dupre and Robin Eschner includes a new setting
  of poetry by the late Steve Fowler\, co-founder of the Sebastopol Peace G
 arden\, soil ecologist\, and community builder. Acorn composer Chris Smith
  will usher listeners into the alchemical mysteries of human composting. J
 oni Mitchell\, Moira Smiley\, and other master songsmiths round out the pr
 ogram. With Acorn's signature approach to melding rich vocal harmony with 
 the values of deep ecology\, this concert will invite reflection on our pl
 ace and purpose on the Earth\, and on the wild intelligence speaking to us
  from beneath our feet.\n"The earth says have a place\; be what that place
  requires\; hear the sound the birds imply and see as deep as ridges go be
 hind each other...Listening\, I think that’s what the earth says."\n– 
 William Stafford.\nTickets
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/acorn-choir
 -the-earth-says
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/", "Press Democrat": "https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Bye Bye Birdie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T213000
UID:260910inV4QrS7oUipomcR5vs5Ow
DESCRIPTION:A joyful\, high-energy musical comedy packed with unforgettabl
 e songs\, humor\, and heart\, "Bye Bye Birdie" is a celebration of youth\,
  fame\, and the delightful chaos that happens when pop culture collides wi
 th small-town life.\n\nFrom the high-energy “The Telephone Hour” to th
 e show-stopping “A Lot of Livin’ to Do\,” the heartfelt “How Lovel
 y to Be a Woman\,” and the iconic “Put On a Happy Face\,” this produ
 ction is filled with classic musical theater moments the whole family can 
 enjoy.\n\nCinnabar Theater's production is directed by Zachary Hasbany\, w
 ith book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, and lyrics by Lee
  Adams\, originally produced by Edward Padula. The show is presented throu
 gh special arrangement with Concord Theatricals.\n\nShow details\n\nCreate
 d by: Book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, lyrics by Lee A
 dams\n\nDirector: Zachary Hasbany\n\nLocation: Sonoma State University –
  Warren Theater\, Ives Hall\, 1801 East Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA 949
 28\n\nPerformance dates: September 18 – October 4\, 2026\; Fridays & Sat
 urdays 7:30pm\, Sundays 2:00pm\n\nEstimated run time: 2 hours\, with one 1
 0-minute intermission\n\nRecommended for families / all ages\n\nASL-Interp
 reted Performance\n\nSunday\, September 27 at 2:00 PM\n\nThis performance 
 will feature American Sign Language \\(ASL\\) interpretation. Patrons who 
 would like seating with a clear view of the ASL interpreter can contact th
 e Box Office at \\(707\\) 763-8920 or boxoffice@cinnabartheater.org.\n\nTi
 ckets: https://ci.ovationtix.com/35211
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Auditorium
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-1?utm_source=sonoma_calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orchestra_sep251", "Press Democrat": "https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-1?utm_source=sonoma_calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orchestra_sep251"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-1?utm_source=sonoma_calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orchestra_sep251"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:SSU Symphony Orchestra
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T210000
UID:260910gmL6msKlwEufpQqQQcv-Ag
DESCRIPTION:Experience the vibrant opening of our season with “French Im
 pressions” on Friday\, September 25! Our concert features four works pre
 miered in Paris during the early part of the twentieth century. We will op
 en with the dazzling *Premiere Rapsodie* for Clarinet and Orchestra with
  soloist and concerto competition winner Diego Borges. Next we'll feature 
 two student conductors\, Alex Roig and Mitchell Thompson\, who will lead t
 he orchestra in a performance of selections from Fauré's enchanting *Dol
 ly* Suite. After the intermission we'll be joined by another concerto com
 petition winner\, Jose Palacios\, featured in Bozza's *Ballade* for Trom
 bone and Orchestra. Concluding the evening will be Stravinsky's 1919 Suite
  from the ballet *Firebird.*
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Joan and Sanford I. Weill Hall
URL:https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-1?utm_source=sonoma
 _calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orche
 stra_sep251
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
