BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net", "Press Democrat": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:ART EXHIBIT:  THE DAYS OF VINES AND ROSES
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260813GtowWVEM7ESawbdPXd0BSw
DESCRIPTION:EPTEMBER ART EXHIBIT:  THE DAYS OF VINES AND ROSES\n\nDate: 
 FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  8/12/26\n\nDATES: August 31 – September 27\, 20
 26\n\nRECEPTION:  SATURDAY\, September 5 – 3 -6 pm Join Donna Schaff
 er and Tosya Shore to celebrate the show and learn about their artistic i
 nspirations.  Refreshments will be served.  \n\nFeatured Artist Donna 
 Schaffer Celebrates Wine Country Beauty in “The Days of Vines and Roses
 ”\n\nSonoma County artist Donna Schaffer unveils her latest collection o
 f oil paintings\, “The Days of Vines and Roses\,” celebrating some of 
 her favorite views of roses blooming among the vineyards\, hills\, and woo
 dlands of Sonoma County. At the heart of the collection is Vines and Trell
 is of Roses\, where glorious pink roses spill across an entrance trellis\,
  set against the orderly rows of a vineyard. In Mini Red Roses Along Viney
 ard\, delicate red roses punctuate the landscape\, creating a lively inter
 play between vineyard rows\, stands of trees\, and the hills beyond. “Li
 ving here in Sonoma County for three decades\, I never tire of its gloriou
 s natural beauty. It is an enduring inspiration and truly a painter’s dr
 eam\,” says Schaffer.\n\nArt has been a focus throughout Schaffer’s li
 fe. She has been painting full time in Dry Creek since the mid-1990s and i
 s particularly known for her paintings of Sonoma County’s wine country. 
 Her work are popular with both locals and visitors who want to bring a bit
  of Sonoma’s beauty and magic into their own homes. Schaffer has been a 
 member of the Upstairs Art Gallery for more than 25 years and has exhibite
 d regionally\, including eight years as an Art Trails artist.\n\nMeet the 
 artist:  Schaffer will be hosting the Gallery on September 3 and 27 from
  11-6 pm.  \n\nStairway Showcase: Tosya Shore — “It’s Black and Wh
 ite with a Splash of Color”\n\nThe Stairway Showcase presents artist Tos
 ya Shore’s “It’s Black and White with a Splash of Color\,” a colle
 ction of watercolors that begins with the fundamentals of composition: red
 ucing an image to its two most essential elements—black and white. Worki
 ng with ink\, a stick\, and a scraper\, Shore roughens the edges of her su
 bjects and strips away unnecessary detail\, allowing light itself—not fo
 rm or precision—to take center stage. Her paintings invite the viewer to
  experience the essence of a scene through contrast\, gesture\, and the ex
 pressive qualities of the medium.\n\nIn addition to her watercolor works\,
  Shore presents paintings inspired by a recent trip to Carmel\, where she 
 picked up oil paint for the first time and explored painting the ocean usi
 ng nothing but a palette knife. The resulting works introduce a vibrant sp
 lash of color and texture into a practice grounded in restraint—new pigm
 ent\, new surface\, yet the same enduring fascination with light over like
 ness.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://tewines.com/pages/experiences/boathouse-wine-food-pairing-experience", "Press Democrat": "https://tewines.com/pages/experiences/boathouse-wine-food-pairing-experience"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://tewines.com/pages/experiences/boathouse-wine-food-pairing-experience"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Boathouse Wine & Food Pairing Experience – Cuvaison and Bran
 dlin Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
UID:260806zcgufh1gXkWUMd7-VDxQ3Q
DESCRIPTION:The Boathouse Wine & Food Pairing Experience invites you on an
  elevated wine journey set in Cuvaison’s stunning waterfront boathouses.
  This luxurious wine tasting experience offers scenic views and a tranquil
  atmosphere\, nestled over the serene reservoir amidst wraparound vineyard
 s. Enjoy a tasting of expertly selected wines paired with seasonal small b
 ites for a curated tasting and pairing.\n\nThe Brandlin Estate Boathouse W
 ine & Food Pairing Experience features 6 wines. The Cuvaison Boathouse Win
 e & Food Pairing Experience features 5 wines.\n\nSet on the edge of the tr
 anquil estate reservoir and surrounded by vineyard views\, the Boathouses 
 offer a peaceful\, private setting for your tasting. Each 120-minute exper
 ience includes a guided flight of estate-grown wines from Cuvaison and Bra
 ndlin Estate\, two estates rooted in Napa Valley history. Together\, they 
 showcase our winemaking philosophy\, from the cool-climate elegance of Los
