BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-robert-dehlingers-alpha-rhythm-kings-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Robert Dehlinger's Alpha Rhythm King
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T170000
UID:260713fcyJUqo1CEmljDtaBgWSGQ
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026. This week's
  lineup features Robert Dehlinger's Alpha Rhythm Kings! Established in 201
 7\, the Alpha Rhythm Kings have created quite a stir with music fans\, cra
 fting an exciting "King Size California sound" that No Depression magazine
  calls "the badge of authenticity." The "swaggering" \\(Washington Post\\)
  ensemble\, led by Rob Dehlinger's "exhilarating" trumpet and "magnetic" v
 ocals \\(Jazz Corner\\)\, has become a favorite with audiences all over th
 e globe\, from Idaho to Indiana\, and Beverly Hills to Budapest. In 2025\,
  Rob Dehlinger and the Alpha Rhythm Kings were invited to Osaka\, Japan\, 
 to represent the United States as performers at the World Expo. Sonoma Sun
 days are free and open to all\, thanks to the generous support of the Sono
 ma Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the McNeely Family Fou
 ndation. Pack your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and meet us on the 
 Plaza!
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-robert-de
 hlingers-alpha-rhythm-kings-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/dear-evan-hansen/", "Press Democrat": "https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/dear-evan-hansen/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/dear-evan-hansen/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Dear Evan Hansen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T163000
UID:260911jZatdyshc06WgRBoKBc9gw
DESCRIPTION:Poignant\, raw\, and of-the-moment\, Dear Evan Hansen pulls ba
 ck the curtain on the profound desire for human connection in the digital 
 age\, offering an empathetic look at the alienation of young people naviga
 ting modern social pressures.\n\nThe story follows Evan\, a high school se
 nior struggling with severe social anxiety who writes motivational letters
  to himself as a therapeutic exercise. When a troubled classmate dies by s
 uicide with one of Evan’s letters in his pocket\, the boy's grieving par
 ents mistakenly believe Evan was his secret best friend. Desperate to comf
 ort them\, Evan plays along\, spiraling into a web of fabricated emails an
 d internet fame before he must ultimately face the truth.\n\nPowered by a 
 critically acclaimed pop-rock score and the sweeping anthems\, Dear Even H
 ansen is a powerful reminder that we are never truly alone. Spreckels is p
 roud to present the North Bay premiere of this six-time Tony Award winning
  musical!
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/dear-evan-hansen/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
