BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cmvineyard.com/visit/", "Press Democrat": "https://cmvineyard.com/visit/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cmvineyard.com/visit/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T170000
UID:260430mTY5DKeXsEK-cENSDmQLkQ
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/16325910"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Children's Wonderland Storytime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T114500
UID:260902CuBArrDqwUSMQoxJB8q22Q
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Children's Wonderland Park for fun\, songs\, and st
 ories every Wednesday at 11:15am! This weekly storytime runs from May 13-O
 ctober 28 thanks to a partnership with GVRD. Location: 360 Glenn St. Valle
 jo\, CA 94590 Free parking in the lot between Children's Wonderland and Va
 llejo Parent Nursery School. Enter through the castle doors guarded by cro
 codiles to the magical world of Children's Wonderland! Climbing features i
 nclude a pirate ship\, train\, "steaming" teapot and much more! Admission:
  Admission to Children's Wonderland is free for Vallejo residents. Visitor
 s from outside of Vallejo may be asked to pay an entrance fee per person. 
 Children must be accompanied by an adult\, and adults may not enter withou
 t a child. Weather: Dress appropriately! The storytelling area has covered
  seating\, and it can be chilly in the mornings during the spring and fall
 . It warms up quickly during the summer. Children's Wonderland will remain
  closed on rainy days. To check for closures\, please visithttps://www.gvr
 d.org/children-s-wonderland. In case of unexpected park closures\, familie
 s are invited to spend the day playing at the Vallejo Springstowne Library
 .
LOCATION:Springstowne Library
URL:https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/16325910
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
