 to_Exhibit_Tom_1980.rev.1787677646.jpg
CATEGORIES:Arts
DESCRIPTION:Chown began his career at SRJC at age 24\, working in the camp
 us photography lab. Over the next 46 years\, he became a familiar presence
  throughout the college community\, documenting the people\, programs and 
 milestones that shaped generations of students and employees.  The exhibit
 ion will trace Chown's evolution as a photographer\, from working with fil
 m and developing photographs in the darkroom to embracing digital photogra
 phy. It also offers a visual history of SRJC\, preserving moments from nea
 rly five decades of college life.  The exhibition will trace Chown's evolu
 tion as a photographer\, from working with film and developing photographs
  in the darkroom to embracing digital photography. It also offers a visual
  history of SRJC\, preserving moments from nearly five decades of college 
 life.  The exhibition is free and open to the public.Location: Robert F. A
 grella Art Gallery\, Doyle Library 1st floor - Santa Rosa CampusFor more i
 nformation\, visit SRJC's Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery website. (https://
 art-gallery.santarosa.edu/exhibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-work)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260825T170827Z
LOCATION:Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23761-artist-walk-through-tom-cho
 wn-46-years-behind-the-lens
