DESCRIPTION:Get ready for an unforgettable night of soulful rhythms and el
 ectrifying performances at the ""Soul Fuse - Sebastopol"" concert! Join us
  at the vibrant Hopmonk Tavern - Sebastopol\, where the atmosphere is as w
 arm and inviting as the music itself. With its rustic charm and lively cro
 wd\, this venue is the perfect backdrop for an evening filled with R&B and
  soul that will have you dancing in your seat. Soul Fuse promises to deliv
 er an experience that resonates deep within your heart\, blending smooth m
 elodies with powerful vocals. Don’t miss out on this chance to immerse y
 ourself in a night of incredible music and community spirit. Grab your fri
 ends and secure your spot for an evening you won’t want to miss!
URL:https://business.sebastopol.org/events/details/soul-fuse-sebastopol
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Chamber of Commerce
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/hal-sparks-friday-night-comedy-in-downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-1992182303899?aff=oddtdtcreator"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Hal Sparks! Friday Night Comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T220000
UID:260822fBIM6qm2ykOfA18nwW39_w
DESCRIPTION:Hal Sparks comes to Downtown Santa Rosa!\n\nVIP TABLES NOW AVA
 ILABLE! Snag a table for 4 with preferred seating\, your own private call 
 button to summon service\, and your first round of beer/cider (or a bottle
  of wine) for only $149!\n\nEvery Friday night hilarious comedians from Th
 e Bay Area and beyond perform at Barrel Proof Lounge. Stick around after f
 or late-night karaoke! Fresh lineup of funny each Friday.\n\nThis Week: Jo
 n Lehre (host) Jeff Klein Headliner: Hal Sparks\n\nHal Sparks is a stand-u
 p comedian\, actor\, musician\, political commentator\, television and rad
 io host and television personality. You know him from his stand-up special
 s as well as his appearances on Queer As Folk \, Talk Soup and more.\n\nAc
 tor/comedian Hal Sparks began his professional career as a teenager in Chi
 cago. As a member of the famed Second City Troupe\, his quick wit and affa
 ble personality quickly gained him recognition and acclaim. In 1987 he was
  named the “Funniest Teenager in Chicago” by The Chicago Sun Times .\n
 \nAfter a successful run with Second City\, Sparks moved to Los Angeles an
 d immediately began performing at numerous comedy clubs\, including The Im
 prov\, The Comedy Store\, The Laugh Factory\, and The Ice House\, as well 
 as at Comic Relief’s American Comedy Festival.\n\nFrom 1999–2000\, Spa
 rks was the host of the Emmy-award winning Talk Soup on E! Entertainment T
 elevision\, winning rave reviews from fans and critics alike. For five sea
 sons\, he co-starred as “Michael Novotny” on the hit Showtime series Q
 ueer as Folk \, based on the controversial and critically acclaimed Britis
 h series. He also starred in his one Showtime stand-up comedy special\, Ch
 armageddon \, in June 2010.\n\nHis numerous television appearances include
  The Tonight Show \, Larry King Live \, Charlie Rose \, Good Morning Ameri
 ca \, The View \, CNN’s Your Money \, Joy Behar \, Politically Incorrect
  \, MTV\, and Jimmy Kimmel Live .\n\n21+ Doors - 7p / Show - 8p $15adv / $
 20door Check out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times
  ahead.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/hal-sparks-friday-night-comedy-in-downtow
 n-santa-rosa-tickets-1992182303899?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
