BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/wild-trail-challenge-2026/", "Press Democrat": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/wild-trail-challenge-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/wild-trail-challenge-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Jack London State Historic Park WILD Trail Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T090000
UID:260803I9dJHb9YAUS-RZClqfO9nQ
DESCRIPTION:On Saturdays from Sept. 5 to Oct. 3\, Jack London State Histor
 ic Park’s WILD Trail Challenge returns for a third year.  This series o
 f five hikes covers every trail in the park for a total of 39.5 miles.  T
 he hikes increase in duration and/or difficulty each week.\n\nParticipants
  can sign up for individual hikes or do them all.\n\nThe price for each hi
 ke is $15.  The park entry fee of $15 per vehicle is waived for these hik
 es.  Those who sign up for all five hikes before Sept. 5 save 20 percent 
 and pay only $60.\n\nHike \\# 1 – Historic Trails\n\nSeptember 5\, 9 a.m
 .-12:30 p.m.  \n\nA great way to warm up. This hike explores the historic
  sites and trails of the park. Navigate both sides of the park to discover
  Jack London’s Beauty Ranch\, London Lake\, and the Wolf House ruins.\n\
 nEasy – moderate hike \\(approximately 4.5 miles roundtrip\\)\n\nHike \\
 # 2 – Ancient Redwood\n\nSeptember 12\, 9 a.m.-1 p.m.   \n\nMeander th
 rough the redwoods and sunny oak woodlands of the park’s three Bridge Tr
 ails \\(Upper\, Lower\, and Fallen\\). The journey leads to the majestic a
 ncient redwood\, fondly known as the Grandmother Tree.\n\nModerate hike \\
 (approximately 6 miles roundtrip\\)\n\nHike \\# 3 – Historic Orchard\n\n
 September 19\, 9 a.m.-1:30 p.m.   \n\nStart Location: Note that this hik
 e does not begin at Jack London State Historic Park\n\nSonoma Developmenta
 l Center\n\nArnold Dr\, Eldridge\, CA 95431\n\nStroll along the blue shore
 s of Fern Lake before reaching the Historic Orchard. Learn about the histo
 ry of the land and the fascinating fruit-bearing crops that thrive there.\
 n\nModerate – Difficult hike \\(approximately 7 miles roundtrip\\)\n\nHi
 ke \\# 4 – Ridge\n\nSeptember 26\, 9 a.m-3:30 p.m.   \n\nDetails: Hike
 rs will gain elevation and an appreciation for the diverse habitats found 
 within the park. They’ll also traverse part of the ever-growing Bay Area
  Ridge Trail.\n\nDifficult hike \\(approximately 12 miles roundtrip\\)\n\n
 Hike \\# 5 – Summit \n\nOctober 3\, 9 a.m.-2:30 p.m.     \n\nA trek
  to the park summit is the perfect way to complete the WILD Trail Challeng
 es.  Climb Sonoma Mountain to enjoy stunning views\, celebrate with fello
 w hikers\, and become a WILD One.\n\nDifficult hike \\(approximately 10 mi
 les roundtrip\\)
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/wild-trail-challenge-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/intfffall26", "Press Democrat": "https://sec.regfox.com/intfffall26"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/intfffall26"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Intermediate Hiking for Fitness Fall 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T130000
UID:260823ugivIT8DikSp03Smk3jwCA
DESCRIPTION:The program leaders will guide you on 8 weekly hikes
  with the challenge increasing each week. Leaders will have grou
 p discussions about gear\, hydration\, hiking poles\, first aid a
 nd pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for Bald Mountain\,
  where hikers can enjoy stunning vistas.\n\nThe following is a l
 ist of possible routes specifically selected for this hiking seri
 es: \n\n1) Sat 9/26 — Creekside + Waterfall loop\, 3.6 miles\,
  750 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 2) Sat 10/03 – Vist
 a Trail loop\, 3.4 miles\, 830 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Bar
 n\\] 3) Sat 10/10 – Hillside to Neptune table + Meadow\, 4.4 
 miles\, 970 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 4) Sat 10/17 
 – Goodspeed to Nattkemper bench\, 3.8 miles\, 1\,240 ft elevati
 on \\[meet @ Goodspeed lot\\] 5) Sat 10/24 – Hillside + Vista
  Trail loop\, 3.6 miles\, 1\,070 ft elevation \\[meet @ White B
 arn\\] 6) Sat 10/31 – False Lake Meadow & Lake Ilsanjo loop i
 n Trionne-Annadel SP\, 6.1 miles\, 670 ft elevation \\[meet @ An
 nadel's Cobblestone Trailhead\\] 7) Sat 11/07 – Fern Lake + Orc
 hard loop in SDC/Jack London SHP\, 5.5 miles\, 1\,460 ft elevati
 on \\[meet @ Walnut & North St inside SDC\; park on Grove St\\
 ] 8) Sat 11/14 – Bald Mtn summit (w/optional Headwaters detour\
 , 5.8 miles)\, 5.1 miles\, 1\,670 ft elevation \\[meet @ White 
 Barn\\]\n\nPlease note these routes are subject to change based o
 n the group and weather\, as the group does hike in light rain
 s. Wear appropriate footwear for rocky or slippery trails\, and 
 layers. Bring water\, and if desired\, a snack. The group will 
 be limited to 35 participants. \n\nThe hiking series costs $80 (
 plus a $10 parking fee per visit. Note that the Sugarloaf Annua
 l Pass is $59 and valid at Sugarloaf and Jack London SHP)\, or
  free-of-cost for participants with a September 2026 or newer Pa
 rk Rx from a Sonoma County Medical Provider.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/intfffall26
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
