SUMMARY:Jack London’s Neighbors: The History of the Sonoma Developmental
  Center
DTSTART:20261008T000000
DTEND:20261008T000000
UID:dacdd54e1b8882befcad368506947da7@jacklondonpark.com
DESCRIPTION:Joinhistorical ecologistAngela Nardo-Morgan for a look at the 
 early history of what became the Sonoma Developmental Center\, from its or
 igins in the late 19th century to it’s closure. The presentation will ex
 plore the founding of the institution at Eldridge in 1891\, its developmen
 t and changing philosophies of care\, and the important role it played in 
 shaping the surrounding Glen Ellen community. The program will also consid
 er the broader history of the area during the lifetimes of Jack and Charm
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park\, 2400 London Ranch Road\, Glen E
 llen\, CA 95442
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-sdc
X-SOURCE:Jack London State Historic Park
END:VEVENT
