DESCRIPTION:checklistMore DetailscommentDescriptionmanage_accountsInstruct
 or InfoinfoFAQprogram overviewThis class introduces the technique of Sashi
 ko mending. With humble beginnings in rural Japan\, Sashiko’s running st
 itch insulated work garments for warmth and longevity. Learn how to patch 
 and repair a rip or hole\, reinforce a worn area\, and prepare distressed 
 textile in order to draw a Sashiko grid and stitch a pattern. Choose from 
 a variety of traditional Sashiko patterns. Bring in one or two garments t
LOCATION:Room 201\, Fiber Arts Studio\, 276 East Napa Street\, Sonoma\, CA
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/sashiko-mending-101726/
