BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/patrick-ball-celtic-harp-story-1"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Patrick Ball: Celtic Harp & Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T210000
UID:6a8c9c573787652e870acdcd@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Step into the enchanting world of\nPatrick Ball\n\, one of the
  premier Celtic harp players in the world and a captivating storyteller wh
 ose performances weave music\, legend\, wit\, and wonder into an unforgett
 able experience.\nWith the crystalline beauty of the Celtic harp as his mu
 sical voice\, Ball brings ancient Irish tales and timeless melodies vividl
 y to life\, transporting audiences to a world of heroes and dreamers\, mys
 tery and mischief\, heartbreak and humor. His masterful playing and gift f
 or storytelling create an evening that is at once intimate\, magical\, and
  deeply human.\nJoin us at Occidental Center for the Arts for a spellbindi
 ng journey through the music and stories of Ireland with a true master of 
 the tradition.\nTickets are $35\, $30 for OCA members. Doors open at 6:30 
 PM\, refreshments available. Art gallery open during event.\nGet Tickets\n
 About Patrick Ball:\nWhether in the stronghold of a Galway chieftain in th
 e years before history began or yesterday in the snug corner of a pub in D
 ublin\, the Irish have always delighted in storytelling. Their passion for
  eloquence and wordplay\, their deep devotion to their mythical past\, the
 ir ability to find joy and humor in a dark world\, and their belief that t
 he supernatural world could appear between one breath and the next made th
 eir stories and the telling of them unrivaled in the world of the oral tra
 dition.\nAnd always\, amidst the storytelling\, there was music. Jigs\, re
 els and haunting airs graced the spaces between the tales. And first among
  Irish instruments\, and the most honored\, was the legendary Celtic harp.
  With its crystalline\, bell-like voice and lavish resonance\, it would so
 othe its listeners and lead them deeper into the realms of the imagination
 .\nIn\nCeltic Harp and Story\nPatrick Ball rekindles the fire and wonder o
 f an evening of Irish storytelling. For in telling the marvelous old tales
  of wit and enchantment\, and in playing the ancient\, brass-strung harp o
 f Ireland\, he not only carries on two of the richest traditions of Celtic
  culture\, but blends them in concert to create “a warm and magical perf
 ormance.”\n“An American master of the Irish instrument\, a peripatetic
  modern day bard\, combining tale-telling\, history and music into a seaml
 ess compound that reaches all ages and types of listeners.”—San Franci
 sco Chronicle\n“It’s rare that we will feature a performer on our fine
  performances season for two consecutive years\, but then Patrick is a rar
 e artist ... The audience was entranced by his harp playing\, amused by hi
 s storytelling. Patrick is a grand man who puts on a great show.”—APAP
  Report / Humboldt State University\n“The SRO audience loved Mr. Ball's 
 performance\, asking when we will be bringing him back. Ball was a delight
  to work with\, very professional\, and he is superb at captivating an aud
 ience.”—APAP Report / Arizona State University\n“Patrick Ball conjur
 ed some Druid magic ... weaving words and music into a spellbinding progra
 m.”—The Blade\, Toledo\, OH
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/patrick-bal
 l-celtic-harp-story-1
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
